  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223522/assets/776278c72c3569eb4ee7bb48c8c544d4731be0378c942256699f5350a15d4b53.png)\n\nThe point $P$ shown above is reflected across the $x$-axis and then translated $3$ units to the left.  Which of the given points is the image of $P$ under this sequence of transformations?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformations.\n\n- Reflecting the point $P$ across the $x$-axis gives the point $F,$ as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223522/assets/782b4ca00a0c7e091873aaafbcc439b9f63b209bd878da3393c81848f2c8f375.png)\n\n- Shifting the point $F$ to the left by $3$ units gives the point $C,$ as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223522/assets/f40099c0f59f3e07fbe505a102a7b7f513dcb8bc36e5abb1382ee8e7b003b9f9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $C.$",
